WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:06.730
Mother, like that sweet lady who climbed the tree with me in Rome...

00:06.730 --> 00:09.610
I wonder if you also have a nostalgic scent about you...

00:09.610 --> 00:13.400
Right now I'm on my way to Salzburg, Austria.

00:13.400 --> 00:17.990
It's only a little further to where the ducal House of Preminger in Vienna is!

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

02:09.150 --> 02:11.610
Salzburg, Austria

02:27.230 --> 02:29.190
﻿It's just a little more until Vienna!

02:29.190 --> 02:32.690
﻿It'd be great if I could find some clues about Mother.

02:40.360 --> 02:42.110
﻿Huh?

02:43.160 --> 02:44.870
﻿Master, what's the problem?

02:45.290 --> 02:46.200
﻿I'm not sure.

02:46.200 --> 02:48.330
﻿It doesn't look like there's a problem with the engine...

02:48.330 --> 02:50.290
﻿I'll look into it some more. Help me out!

02:50.290 --> 02:52.080
﻿Roger that!

02:53.630 --> 02:55.880
Ah, this has to be it!

02:55.880 --> 02:57.050
﻿What is it, what is it?

02:57.460 --> 03:00.420
﻿Some of the teeth on the gear have broken off.

03:00.430 --> 03:04.050
﻿There's nothing we can do about this until we can buy a new one...

03:04.050 --> 03:05.850
﻿It'll take a week?!

03:05.850 --> 03:10.640
﻿We don't carry automobile gears here, so we ll have to send away for them...

03:10.640 --> 03:14.610
﻿I want to hurry and get to Vienna! Can't you make it any sooner?-

03:14.610 --> 03:18.480
﻿Even if you ask that of me. I'll need at least a week to look over it...

03:18.490 --> 03:23.990
﻿There's no helping it. We ll have to wait in this city performing for a week.

03:24.490 --> 03:26.700
﻿Don't be too disappointed, Nadja.

03:26.700 --> 03:29.370
﻿One week will pass by in no time!

03:29.370 --> 03:31.120
﻿Yeah...

03:34.420 --> 03:38.210
﻿Here we go. And one and two...

03:43.510 --> 03:45.300
﻿What are you kids doing?

03:45.300 --> 03:49.310
﻿What are we doing? We're putting up posters for our Dandelion Troupe...

03:49.310 --> 03:51.310
﻿The Dandelion Troupe?

03:51.310 --> 03:52.940
I'﻿ve never heard of any troupe by that name.

03:52.940 --> 03:54.810
﻿This is our first time to Salzburg.

03:54.810 --> 03:57.270
﻿Hey! What are you doing over there?!

03:57.270 --> 03:58.940
﻿N-Nothing at all...

03:58.940 --> 04:02.650
﻿You were just peeking into the mayor's manor, weren't you?!

04:02.650 --> 04:04.110
I-It's just ﻿that...

04:04.110 --> 04:07.740
﻿I heard rumours that the phantom thief Black Rose sent out a new advanced notice...

04:07.740 --> 04:11.750
﻿So I just thought the mayor might be a little panicky...

04:11.750 --> 04:13.660
﻿The Black Rose?

04:19.110 --> 04:24.110
Danger Lurks! The Black Rose's Life on the Line

04:25.390 --> 04:27.090
﻿We're back!

04:27.350 --> 04:28.550
﻿Welcome back.

04:28.560 --> 04:31.180
﻿Huh? What's this?

04:31.180 --> 04:33.060
﻿Isn't this quite the luxurious feast?

04:33.350 --> 04:35.480
﻿Someone from city hall just stopped by, actually.

04:35.480 --> 04:39.480
﻿They invited us to perform at a charity concert three days from now...

04:39.480 --> 04:41.980
﻿...for children with no relatives and the elderly.

04:41.990 --> 04:44.240
﻿It looks like the fliers we handed out...

04:44.240 --> 04:47.450
﻿...really caught the eyes of the mayor whom asked for us personally to come, huh?

04:47.450 --> 04:50.240
﻿But if it's for charity, then we can't receive any money...

04:50.240 --> 04:52.700
﻿Actually, it seems like the mayor is a very kind man.

04:52.700 --> 04:55.210
﻿And he gave us an advanced payment for our performance fee.

04:55.210 --> 04:56.540
﻿So that's what this is all about-!

04:56.540 --> 04:57.670
﻿Yeah.

04:57.670 --> 05:03.050
﻿That's strange... why would the Black Rose go to the manor of a person like that?

05:16.480 --> 05:18.650
﻿He ran off that way!

05:23.360 --> 05:25.240
﻿The Black Rose?!

05:31.280 --> 05:33.990
﻿The Black Rose wasn't down this way!

05:34.000 --> 05:36.290
﻿Damn it! You guys take a look out over there!

05:36.290 --> 05:38.210
﻿Yeah!

06:00.270 --> 06:02.020
﻿Nadja...

06:02.650 --> 06:04.480
﻿Keith!

06:04.480 --> 06:05.940
﻿How do you know my name...?

06:05.940 --> 06:10.950
﻿Francis told me you were his older twin brother.

06:14.700 --> 06:19.210
﻿Nadja, until I say it's all right to look up, keep your face hidden.

06:19.210 --> 06:21.380
﻿Do you understand me? Do as I say.

06:21.380 --> 06:23.290
﻿But what about you?

06:25.050 --> 06:27.420
﻿Someone's over here!

06:27.420 --> 06:28.760
﻿What's all this ruckus about?

06:28.760 --> 06:31.260
﻿What are you two doing out here this late at night?

06:31.260 --> 06:34.930
﻿I can see that the police of Salzburg are quite insensitive.

06:34.930 --> 06:37.850
﻿W-What?! Who are you?!

06:37.850 --> 06:41.190
﻿My name is Francis Harcourt.

06:41.400 --> 06:43.900
﻿Francis... Harcourt?

06:43.900 --> 06:46.110
﻿I've heard that name somewhere before...

06:46.110 --> 06:49.150
﻿Could it be that he was at the tree-planting ceremony last year...?

06:49.150 --> 06:51.450
﻿The one from the Marquess of Harcourt?

06:51.740 --> 06:54.450
﻿You all were quite a help last year, thank you.

06:54.450 --> 06:56.950
﻿Excuse us for having disturbed you tonight!

06:56.950 --> 06:59.540
﻿As long as you understand, that's more than enough.

06:59.540 --> 07:01.330
﻿Shall we go then, my honey?

07:01.330 --> 07:04.500
﻿"M-My honey"?!

07:04.790 --> 07:06.300
﻿Hey, let's look elsewhere.

07:06.300 --> 07:07.960
﻿All right.

07:11.640 --> 07:14.390
﻿What's up with that "my honey" bit?

07:14.390 --> 07:20.310
﻿Then would you prefer me calling you "my little Rosebud"?

07:23.650 --> 07:26.900
﻿Wait up a little. What are you so mad about?

07:26.900 --> 07:30.440
﻿I've already apologized for treating you like my girlfriend.

07:30.450 --> 07:31.570
﻿That's not all!

07:31.950 --> 07:36.780
﻿I don't think you have any right to use Francis' name just to escape from the police!

07:36.790 --> 07:38.580
﻿You were mad about something like that?

07:38.580 --> 07:40.000
﻿"Something like that"?

07:40.000 --> 07:43.960
﻿If they get suspicious over Francis, what are you going to do then?

07:47.460 --> 07:50.340
﻿Why do you keep on committing crimes like this?

07:50.340 --> 07:54.590
﻿I really don't think there's too much difference between what Francis and I do.

07:54.590 --> 07:56.510
﻿It's completely different!

07:56.760 --> 07:59.220
﻿Always keeping himself out of harms way,

07:59.220 --> 08:02.230
﻿looking down upon the masses from a nobles standpoint...

08:02.230 --> 08:05.020
﻿A hypocrite busying himself with charity.

08:05.020 --> 08:08.480
﻿I think what I'm doing is much better.

08:09.480 --> 08:12.570
﻿Francis is not a hypocrite.

08:12.570 --> 08:15.610
﻿He's hurting himself by pushing him to the limits of what he can do...

08:15.620 --> 08:17.570
﻿Even if you may call him a hypocrite...

08:17.580 --> 08:18.950
﻿Even if he gets all beaten up...

08:18.950 --> 08:22.370
﻿He continues to push down the path he believes is right.

08:22.960 --> 08:28.290
﻿At the very least, I think what he does is much greater than the thievery you do!

08:30.590 --> 08:32.720
﻿Even though you're brothers...

08:32.720 --> 08:35.840
﻿Even though you both have the same goals...

08:35.840 --> 08:38.760
﻿Why is it that you and Francis are so different?

08:38.760 --> 08:43.600
﻿In the dark, wherever you find light, you'll also find shadow.

08:43.600 --> 08:46.440
﻿Even here at the Mirabell Palace as well.

08:46.440 --> 08:49.270
﻿Right now it's nothing more than a famous sight for sightseers.

08:49.270 --> 08:54.530
﻿But in the 17th century, the archbishop who had absolute authority over this area...

08:54.530 --> 08:59.240
﻿...had this building erected for his mistress and his children.

08:59.660 --> 09:03.410
﻿He did things such as this, all the while preaching the Word of God.

09:03.410 --> 09:05.210
﻿How does that relate to you and Francis?

09:05.210 --> 09:07.000
﻿It's the same case.

09:07.000 --> 09:10.750
﻿Francis was brought up looking only at the light of our mother...

09:10.750 --> 09:14.720
﻿Whereas I learned of her through her shadow.

09:14.720 --> 09:16.340
﻿Therein lies our difference.

09:16.340 --> 09:18.760
﻿Her shadow?

09:19.140 --> 09:22.140
﻿She was a kind and very enthusiastic person towards her charity work.

09:22.140 --> 09:24.350
﻿Francis admired her for that.

09:24.350 --> 09:27.690
﻿That's because he only saw her outside appearance.

09:28.270 --> 09:31.610
I was also made to go to her charity events.

09:31.610 --> 09:36.570
﻿but Francis always looked at her as if she were the Sun and helped her.

09:36.570 --> 09:39.200
﻿But I couldn't do that.

09:39.200 --> 09:41.160
﻿Why do you think?

09:43.040 --> 09:47.960
﻿It's true that our mother was a very kind person who would be respected by all...

09:47.960 --> 09:52.840
﻿But, in front of our father, she was a pitiful woman.

09:54.590 --> 09:56.880
﻿How many times do I have to tell you until you understand?!

09:56.880 --> 09:59.340
I ﻿won't allow any of that!

09:59.340 --> 10:01.300
﻿Not just within England's borders...

10:01.300 --> 10:04.470
﻿But there are so many unblessed children across the world!

10:04.470 --> 10:06.850
﻿Please, for those children as well...

10:06.850 --> 10:09.230
﻿Your charity work is good enough within this country.

10:09.650 --> 10:13.440
﻿That aside, we have many important parties upcoming this month.

10:13.440 --> 10:18.360
﻿As the Marchioness of Harcourt, you should focus more on those!

10:18.360 --> 10:20.200
﻿But...

10:21.530 --> 10:22.620
﻿What is it?

10:22.620 --> 10:27.700
﻿Milord, one of the Earl Hewitt's servants is here requesting an audience.

10:27.710 --> 10:29.540
﻿Understood.

10:29.870 --> 10:31.830
﻿Dear!

10:38.930 --> 10:42.140
﻿Mother, are you all right?

10:42.890 --> 10:44.930
﻿Keith...

10:57.740 --> 11:00.650
﻿What you're saying is right, Mother!

11:00.660 --> 11:04.780
﻿You should just go to France or Italy or wherever you'd like!

11:04.780 --> 11:08.330
﻿If I could, how wonderful it would be...

11:08.330 --> 11:11.330
﻿You don't have to listen to what Father says.

11:11.330 --> 11:16.090
﻿It's impossible. If I don't have your father's approval, I can't.

11:16.090 --> 11:19.670
﻿That's just weird. If you know it's right, then you should.

11:19.670 --> 11:23.140
﻿In this house, what your father says is absolute.

11:23.140 --> 11:25.720
﻿You cannot go against him.

11:25.720 --> 11:27.680
﻿Mother...

11:27.970 --> 11:31.940
﻿That's been the custom in noble houses since long before.

11:31.940 --> 11:35.770
﻿No one may disobey him.

11:38.780 --> 11:45.320
﻿After that event, Mother hardly ever left the house besides for charity events.

11:45.330 --> 11:48.790
﻿She used to love taking strolls and having picnics so much.

11:51.210 --> 11:53.750
﻿Because of that ridiculous noble custom,

11:53.750 --> 11:56.840
﻿my mother kept on getting crushed more and more...

12:02.300 --> 12:08.640
﻿...and at a young age of 28, she departed for Heaven.

12:11.430 --> 12:17.020
﻿I hated my father and the noble society that bound my mother to their "customs",

12:17.020 --> 12:19.070
﻿and ran away from home.

12:19.480 --> 12:22.280
﻿I never knew such a thing happened...

12:22.280 --> 12:27.370
﻿All those nobles out there are wearing a million more masks than I do.

12:27.370 --> 12:30.450
﻿That's why, for you, I...

12:32.040 --> 12:32.790
Wh﻿at is it?

12:32.790 --> 12:34.250
﻿What happened to your brooch?!

12:34.250 --> 12:36.960
﻿Th-That is...

12:37.960 --> 12:41.710
﻿When I went to Egypt... it was stolen.

12:41.710 --> 12:46.130
﻿What did you say?! To think that I told you to ALWAYS keep it safe!

13:09.580 --> 13:11.080
﻿I'm sorry...

13:11.080 --> 13:12.620
﻿When I first met you,

13:12.620 --> 13:16.500
﻿if you remember those two detectives who tried to steal my brooch...

13:16.500 --> 13:18.670
﻿Those two?!

13:18.670 --> 13:23.300
﻿More than likely, they're detectives hired by someone in the Ducal House of Preminger.

13:23.300 --> 13:26.630
﻿Keith, how do you know about the Ducal House of Preminger?

13:26.630 --> 13:29.850
﻿That night, when I saved you from those two,

13:29.850 --> 13:33.970
﻿I noticed the little trick on the ring inside your brooch.

13:42.230 --> 13:43.780
﻿This is...!

13:43.780 --> 13:47.450
﻿I thought I had seen that familiar swan symbol before, and once I researched it...

13:47.450 --> 13:50.990
﻿I learned that it was part of the coat of arms for the Ducal House of Preminger.

13:50.990 --> 13:52.200
﻿So you did too...

13:52.200 --> 13:55.620
﻿Nadja, you'd best stay away from the Ducal House of Preminger.

13:55.620 --> 13:56.790
﻿Why?

13:56.790 --> 13:58.870
﻿Right now there's a problem going on with the next successor...

13:58.880 --> 14:01.380
﻿It seems like there's some unrest.

14:01.380 --> 14:03.880
﻿It's too dangerous to walk into that.

14:03.880 --> 14:05.090
﻿Don't go to Vienna.

14:05.090 --> 14:06.050
﻿No!

14:06.260 --> 14:07.720
﻿Nadja...

14:07.720 --> 14:10.930
﻿I want to meet my mother no matter what!

14:10.930 --> 14:13.640
﻿What do you plan to do by meeting her?

14:13.640 --> 14:15.560
﻿Do you want to become a noble?

14:15.560 --> 14:20.400
﻿It doesn't matter whether or not my mother is a noble, I wouldn't care!

14:20.400 --> 14:23.900
﻿I just want to meet her!

14:25.230 --> 14:27.860
﻿I understand, Nadja.

14:39.980 --> 14:40.850
Herman's Manor

14:54.180 --> 14:56.100
﻿Put the napkin on your lap.

14:56.100 --> 14:57.020
﻿Yes!

14:57.020 --> 15:00.140
﻿For your knife, fork, and spoon, you start by taking the one farthest away from you.

15:00.140 --> 15:01.810
﻿Yes, Lady Hilda.

15:01.810 --> 15:04.610
﻿Nadja, don't call me "Lady Hilda."

15:04.610 --> 15:08.400
﻿You're the person who will be the next in line for the Ducal House of Preminger.

15:08.400 --> 15:10.450
﻿Please call me Aunt Hilda.

15:10.450 --> 15:12.160
﻿Yes, Aunt Hilda!

15:12.530 --> 15:13.950
﻿Yes, that'd be just fine.

15:13.950 --> 15:14.530
﻿Yes!

15:14.530 --> 15:19.500
﻿Sir, a Mr. Rosso and Mr. Bianco are here to see you.

15:20.960 --> 15:23.460
﻿Good work. Let's talk upstairs in my room.

15:23.460 --> 15:25.420
﻿Uncle Herman.

15:25.420 --> 15:30.010
﻿To have someone as kind as Aunt Hilda teach me the manners of nobility,

15:30.010 --> 15:32.340
﻿makes me extremely happy.

15:32.340 --> 15:33.840
﻿Thank you so very much!

15:33.850 --> 15:39.220
﻿Oh, Nadja... you're going to be our relative so it's natural.

15:39.230 --> 15:41.350
﻿Shall we take a small break then?

15:41.350 --> 15:44.230
﻿Yes, Aunt Hilda!

15:50.110 --> 15:52.820
﻿That girl's quite the golden egg, huh?

15:52.820 --> 15:56.580
﻿Yes. She even brought the clothes from the orphanage she was brought up in.

15:56.580 --> 15:59.870
﻿Quite a fearsome girl, isn't she?

16:03.830 --> 16:05.130
﻿W-Who's there?!

16:05.130 --> 16:06.920
﻿The phantom thief, Black Rose?

16:06.920 --> 16:08.670
﻿I'll be taking this brooch.

16:08.670 --> 16:11.260
﻿Give that brooch back!

16:11.260 --> 16:13.550
﻿You're a nuisance! Get out of my way!

16:16.550 --> 16:18.720
I ﻿won't let you escape.

16:24.940 --> 16:27.480
﻿Nadja!

16:27.480 --> 16:31.360
﻿The evening dew is bad for your body. Come back into your room.

16:31.360 --> 16:34.070
﻿Yes, Aunt Hilda!

16:34.070 --> 16:35.860
﻿That's not Nadja.

16:35.870 --> 16:40.240
﻿If you move an inch, consider yourself dead.

16:40.240 --> 16:42.620
﻿Hey, hurry and bind him.

16:42.620 --> 16:44.710
﻿Y-Yes, sir!

16:47.460 --> 16:49.920
﻿Mayor! Mayor!

16:49.920 --> 16:53.260
﻿What are you going to do about the charity concert?!

17:00.970 --> 17:05.440
﻿Besides the elderly and children invited, hardly anyone else is here...

17:05.440 --> 17:07.440
﻿And this is the concert sponsored by the mayor

17:07.440 --> 17:11.190
﻿who was supposed to have something stolen by the phantom thief Black Rose...

17:11.190 --> 17:17.570
﻿The people must have smelt something fishy about the charity...

17:18.030 --> 17:21.120
﻿It looks like all the other performers canceled too.

17:21.540 --> 17:23.120
﻿Then what's going to happen to the concert?

17:23.500 --> 17:25.040
﻿It'll probably be canceled too...

17:25.040 --> 17:26.120
﻿No way!

17:26.120 --> 17:28.540
﻿When I thought I would show them my cool self today too!

17:28.920 --> 17:31.710
﻿Oh well. Don't get so disappointed.

17:32.210 --> 17:33.760
﻿Please wait!

17:33.760 --> 17:37.930
﻿It's too cruel to send every one home who've especially come out for the concert!

17:37.930 --> 17:41.050
﻿But it's already something that's been decided...

17:41.600 --> 17:44.660
﻿Master! Let's just do our show!

17:44.660 --> 17:45.560
You're right!

17:45.560 --> 17:50.560
﻿It's the Dandelion Troupe's motto to see through with any job we've accepted!

17:50.570 --> 17:52.860
﻿It'll be fine with just us alone!

17:52.860 --> 17:56.530
﻿For the people here, let's show off our tricks with all our heart!

17:56.530 --> 17:58.110
Yeah!

17:58.110 --> 18:02.280
﻿Now everyone, it s time to begin!

18:02.700 --> 18:06.750
﻿It's the very fun theme song of the Dandelion Troupe!

18:06.730 --> 18:13.780
Hello hello, how are you, people of England?

18:13.780 --> 18:20.660
Bonjour bonjour, how are you, people of France?

18:20.660 --> 18:29.170
Buenas tardes, how are you, people of Spain?

18:32.820 --> 18:34.150
﻿There!

18:34.150 --> 18:36.150
﻿And take this too!

18:39.030 --> 18:42.200
﻿Now, hurry and confess!

18:42.200 --> 18:45.120
﻿Why did you try to steal the brooch?’

18:45.120 --> 18:47.700
﻿What are you planning?!

18:49.790 --> 18:52.670
﻿You're too lenient! I'll do it.

18:52.790 --> 18:54.130
﻿Tear off his shirt.

18:54.130 --> 18:55.000
﻿Yes, sir!

18:57.300 --> 18:59.050
﻿Spill! Let's hear it!

18:59.050 --> 19:01.840
﻿Take this! And this!

19:17.150 --> 19:20.860
﻿How stubborn!

19:29.250 --> 19:33.420
﻿Oh? Since you've caused such a fuss in society,

19:33.420 --> 19:35.500
﻿I thought you'd be a little scarier looking.

19:35.500 --> 19:38.130
﻿But you're quite the pretty boy, aren't you

19:38.130 --> 19:40.670
﻿Y-You little...!

20:38.360 --> 20:40.610
﻿Keep a watch over him so he can't escape.

20:40.610 --> 20:42.490
﻿Yes, sir!

20:43.740 --> 20:46.950
﻿Lord Herman is a scary man.

20:46.950 --> 20:50.740
